<article class="env-remark" id="113A1F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/113A1F">Remark <span data-tag="113A1F">5.2.9.7</span>.</a> In other words, $\calC ^0$ strongly generates $\calC $ if and only if the identity functor $\id _{\calC }$ is a left Kan extension of $\id _{\calC } | \calC ^{0}$. It follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/83A0A3" data-tag="83A0A3">4.3.2.8</a> that if $\calC ^{0} \subseteq \calC ^{1} \subseteq \calC $ are full subcategories and $\calC ^{0}$ strongly generates $\calC $, then $\calC ^{1}$ also strongly generates $\calC $. </p>
